 ## 11. Handoff and ongoing operations
 
+After all release postflight checks, or a verified healthy rollback, release this
+session's deployment lock before resuming the previously active backup timers.
+Keep the shell/array from section 3. Never blindly enable timers or resume from an
+unresolved restricted/migration state:
+
+```bash
+flock -u 9
+exec 9>&-
+if (( ${#PLIEGO_BACKUP_TIMERS_TO_RESUME[@]} )); then
+  systemctl start "${PLIEGO_BACKUP_TIMERS_TO_RESUME[@]}"
+fi
+```
+
+Confirm next UTC firings, both DB/invoice completion markers and external
+heartbeats. A successful unit exit can be a deploy-lock skip; it is insufficient
+without fresh receipts/remote run markers. Record pause/drain/resume times and any
+skipped/overdue run. Retain keys, receipts and locked remote objects on rollback.
+[Backup production operations](../operations/2026-11-05-backup-production-operations.md)
